  "description": "CR 508.5 / 506.4e / 310.9d whole cards: Gaea's Liege attacking, as a planeswalker, a Siege that is only a battle now counts its protector's Forests, not its controller's",
  "note": "Three seats, every opponent defending (CR 802.2). bob's Invasion of Dominaria, carol protecting it, is made a 5/5 artifact creature (Liquimetal Coating, Skilled Animator) and a planeswalker (Planeswalkerificate) on his turn. On alice's turn Gaea's Liege, 2/2 on her two Forests, attacks it as a planeswalker and counts bob's one Forest. Magnetic Theft then attaches Luxior, Giada's Gift: no planeswalker, still a battle being attacked (CR 506.4e), so carol, its protector, is the defending player relative to it (CR 310.9d), and the Liege's layer 7b effect counts her three Forests (CR 508.5).",
